Q: How to clear focus of BasicTextField upon clicking somewhere else in Compose Multiplatform? A: <p>Using your focusManager (which is enough alone) and keyboardController</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>    val keyboardController = LocalSoftwareKeyboardController.current
    val focusManager = LocalFocusManager.current
</code></pre>
<p>Then, in your parent box (or whatever layout you are using), add <code>pointerInput</code> to the modifier:</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>    Box(
        modifier = Modifier
            .pointerInput(Unit) {
                detectTapGestures(
                    onTap = {
                        focusManager.clearFocus()
                        keyboardController?.hide()
                    }
                )
            }
    ) {
        // Your code ...
    }
</code></pre>

Q: CollectionGroupQuery but limit search to subcollections under a particular document A: <p>@samthecodingman's answer is fantastic, but I think there's one more useful thing to add here. I used his answer to develop a helper function that streamlines building a query for this.</p>
<p>You provide the standard <code>collectionGroup</code> name and a <code>pathPrefix</code>, and it returns a query to you. It works with <code>pathPrefix</code>'s that point to documents or collections.</p>
<p>If you'd prefer to have a helper function you can easily copy and paste in, then here it is below in Typescript:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>/**
 * Performs a collection group query across all similarly named collections in
 * the database. Uses a path prefix input to create a filter that rejects all
 * documents that do not have the path prefix on the server-side, reducing
 * data transfer and client-side processing.
 *
 * As of 2025-12-30, Firestore requires the path prefix to have an even number
 * of segments. Without this, the query will fail. Therefore, if you provide a
 * path prefix that points to a collection, the function will find the first
 * and last document in the collection and use them to create the start and
 * end path prefixes.
 *
 * @param {string} collectionGroup - The collection group to query. This is
 * the name you would usually use to query a single collection.
 * @param {string} pathPrefix - The path prefix to use for the query. Each
 * document has a path stored under the `__name__` field. This is the path to
 * the document from the root of the database. If a document does not have the
 * path prefix, it will be rejected by the server-side filter.
 * @param {admin.firestore.Firestore} db - The firestore database instance.
 * Dependency injection for easier testing.
 * @returns {Promise&lt;admin.firestore.Query&lt;admin.firestore.DocumentData&gt;&gt;} A
 * query object that can be extended and modified with additional filters.
 * @throws {Error} If the pathPrefix points to a collection, but the
 * collection is empty.
 * ```
 */
export async function collectionGroupWithPathPrefixQuery(
  collectionGroup: string,
  pathPrefix: string,
  db: admin.firestore.Firestore
): Promise&lt;admin.firestore.Query&lt;admin.firestore.DocumentData&gt;&gt; {
  let startPathPrefix = pathPrefix;
  let endPathPrefix = pathPrefix + &quot;\uf8ff&quot;; // \uf8ff is the high Unicode character for inclusive upper bound

  const pathParts = pathPrefix.split(&quot;/&quot;);

  if (pathParts.length % 2 !== 0) {
    const collectionRef = db.collection(pathPrefix);

    const firstSnapshot = await collectionRef.orderBy(&quot;__name__&quot;).limit(1).get();

    // Requires an index to be built
    const lastSnapshot = await collectionRef.orderBy(&quot;__name__&quot;, &quot;desc&quot;).limit(1).get();

    if (firstSnapshot.empty || lastSnapshot.empty) {
      throw new Error(&quot;Collection is empty&quot;);
    }

    startPathPrefix = firstSnapshot.docs[0].ref.path;
    endPathPrefix = lastSnapshot.docs[0].ref.path;
  }

  const query = db.collectionGroup(collectionGroup).orderBy(&quot;__name__&quot;).startAt(startPathPrefix).endAt(endPathPrefix);

  return query;
}
</code></pre>
